## Why this is the correct invariant

- `URL.Path` is the canonical, decoded resource identity and is what `gorilla/mux` matches and handlers observe.
- The signature deliberately covers `Method`, `Path`, and unix-seconds timestamp only. `RawQuery` is excluded, so it must not be pulled in via `RequestURI()`/`EscapedPath()`.
- Sharing one `canonicalPayload` helper prevents client/server drift for any future encoding rule.

