## 5. Takeaways

- A preflight must invoke the **same** acceptance function as the runtime, not a re-implemented approximation. Skipping the cheap gate is what allowed a real embed to succeed while the report said nothing was usable.
- Model the selection mode (`auto`) separately from concrete provider ids; never pass a mode through `getProvider()`.
- Make the summary a derived invariant (`ok ⇔ any usable`), not an independently-tracked boolean, so success and the narrative cannot disagree.
- Trap tests (a healthy-gate failure paired with an embed that *would* succeed) are the cheapest way to prove the gate is actually load-bearing and ordered before the request.

