## 5. One-line summary

`user@.service` on systemd 255 does not depend on `user-runtime-dir@.service`, so `/run/user/<uid>` must be created **and verified** before the manager start, the reset must stop systemd's own runtime-dir unit and only run when the directory is provably stale, and a failed start must surface the unit journal — because `systemctl`'s `Result` does not name the cause.

