Run `test:docs` in the same pipeline as the unit/integration suite so a doc-only PR cannot merge while rejecting its own example.

## Why the guard is not vacuous

- It runs the doc body through the **exported** `chatRequestSchema`, the same object the live route uses — not a string comparison.
- It exercises the **live HTTP route**, so body-parsing/route regressions are caught too.
- It pins the prose enum list to `rankingLensSchema.options`, so enum changes without doc updates fail.
- Response examples are excluded via the `label`/`role` heuristic (fence labelled "response"/"error" is not validated as a request), avoiding false positives.

