Expected results from the verified fix: all documented keys except the named exemptions resolve with `source=flag` (the reference run reported 78 of 83 addressable, 5 explicitly named exemptions); unknown key stays `TROUBLE-LIFECYCLE-001` / exit 13; one-dash typo is a loud usage error; `--config-path` correctly does not resolve; and a newly added registry key with no flag spelling and no named exemption fails `TestEveryRegistryKeyAddressable`.

## One-line summary

Stop letting the outer `flag.FlagSet` be a whitelist. Split argv with `splitDaemonArgs` (own forms only), forward everything else verbatim to the registry resolver, reject orphan one-dash tokens, print help from the registry, and lock it in with a code-derived key-inventory test plus a named exemption table.

